Feature: the VFS picks the device with the LONGEST matching mount path (nested mounts)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0012-vfs-longest-mount-wins.patch
Status:     local patch (a small feature; without nested mounts nothing changes)

WHY
  VirtualFileSystem::ResolvePath took the FIRST registered device whose
  mount path the (symlink-resolved) path starts with. A device mounted
  inside another one's tree, e.g. a host folder at
  \Device\Harddisk0\Partition1\crashmom inside the game's drive
  (\Device\Harddisk0\Partition1, registered first by Runtime::SetupVfs),
  was never reached: D:\crashmom\x went to the game folder.

WHAT
  ResolvePath scans all devices and keeps the one with the longest mount
  path that matches (same prefix rule as before; ties keep the first
  registered). Without nested mounts it is the same device as before.

HOW WE FOUND / CHECKED IT (2026-10-03)
  The port serves changed copies of game data files (src/data/data_patcher.h:
  the in-game menus package with the name entry keyboard, the front end's
  tree) as loose files the game opens as D:\crashmom\<file>. With the first-match rule the open of that
  path failed (NtCreateFile ... 0xc000000f, looked up in the game folder);
  with this patch the host folder device answers and the game loads the
  file. Boot, menus and a level load unchanged otherwise (0 errors).

diff --git a/src/filesystem/virtual_file_system.cpp b/src/filesystem/virtual_file_system.cpp
index 682b23d..584db74 100644
--- a/src/filesystem/virtual_file_system.cpp
+++ b/src/filesystem/virtual_file_system.cpp
@@ -115,10 +115,18 @@ Entry* VirtualFileSystem::ResolvePath(const std::string_view path) {
     normalized_path = resolved_path;
   }
 
-  // Find the device.
-  auto it = std::find_if(devices_.cbegin(), devices_.cend(), [&](const auto& d) {
-    return rex::string::utf8_starts_with_case(normalized_path, d->mount_path());
-  });
+  // Find the device: the one with the LONGEST mount path the path starts
+  // with, so a device can be mounted inside another one's tree (e.g. a host
+  // folder at \Device\Harddisk0\Partition1\crashmom inside the game's drive).
+  // Without nested mounts this is the same device as before (the first
+  // match); ties keep the first registered.
+  auto it = devices_.cend();
+  for (auto d = devices_.cbegin(); d != devices_.cend(); ++d) {
+    if (rex::string::utf8_starts_with_case(normalized_path, (*d)->mount_path()) &&
+        (it == devices_.cend() || (*d)->mount_path().size() > (*it)->mount_path().size())) {
+      it = d;
+    }
+  }
   if (it == devices_.cend()) {
     REXFS_WARN("VFS: '{}' -> [no device]", path);
     // Supress logging the error for ShaderDumpxe:\CompareBackEnds as this is
